  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n  The `GaugeManager._updateForAfterDistribution()` function uses current voting weights instead of epoch-snapshot weights when calculating reward distributions. This creates a serious timing vulnerability between `update_period()` and `distribute()` calls.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _updateForAfterDistribution(address _gauge) private {\n    address _pool = poolForGauge[_gauge];\n    //uint256 _supplied = weightsPerEpoch[_time][_pool];  //  Commented out\n    uint256 _supplied = IVoter(voter).weights(_pool);    //  Uses current weights\n    \n    if (_supplied > 0) {\n        uint256 _supplyIndex = supplyIndex[_gauge];\n        uint256 _index = index;\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = _index;\n        uint256 _delta = _index - _supplyIndex;\n        if (_delta > 0) {\n            uint256 _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18;\n            if (isAlive[_gauge]) {\n                claimable[_gauge] += _share;  //  Never executed if weight = 0\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;  //  Index update without rewards\n    }\n}\n```\n\n based commented-out line (`weightsPerEpoch[_time][_pool]`) tells me the development team was aware of the need for epoch-based weight tracking, but this functionality was never implemented. The codebase lacks any `weightsPerEpoch` mapping or snapshot mechanism.\n\nTo be more specific consider the following attack permissionless sequence scenario:\n\nEpoch N, Gauge A has significant voting weight (e.g., 50,000 weight)\nEpoch N+1 begins, Attacker (or any user) calls `Minter.update_period()`\n    This function is publicly callable with no access control \n    Increases `GaugeManager.index` based on current `totalWeight`\n    Transfers emission tokens to `GaugeManager`\nBefore `distribute()` is called Voters call `VoterV3.reset()` to remove votes\n    `reset()` has `onlyNewEpoch` modifier, allowing calls in new epochs (line 122)\n    Reduces gauge weight to 0 or near-0\n`distribute()` is called Uses current weight (0) instead of epoch weight\n    Line 376 `_supplied = 0`\n    Line 378 `if (_supplied > 0)` evaluates to FALSE\n    Line 393 `supplyIndex[_gauge] = index` updates without accumulating rewards\nResult Epoch rewards permanently locked in `GaugeManager`\n\n\n### the impact can be critical as it leads to\n\n Complete Loss of Epoch Rewards, Gauges with modified weights between `update_period()` and `distribute()` receive zero rewards despite having weight during the reward period\nPermanent Fund Lockup, Rewards become permanently stuck in `GaugeManager` contract with no recovery mechanism\nProtocol Insolvency Risk, Over multiple epochs, substantial emission tokens can accumulate as stuck funds\nVoter Disincentivization, veNFT holders lose rewards through no fault of their own, breaking protocol incentive mechanism\n\nAn attacker can also exploit this in reverse for Reward Theft:\n Epoch N Minimal votes on gauge B\n `update_period()` called (low totalWeight, high index increase per gauge)\n Attacker front-runs `distribute()` and votes heavily for gauge B\n Gauge B receives disproportionate rewards meant for other gauges\n\nthis also violated some invariants:\n Proportionality: \"Emissions allocated to gauges must be strictly proportional to their effective weight snapshots\"\n Epoch Boundary Consistency: \"Weight snapshots take effect strictly at epoch boundaries. Updates in one epoch must not retroactively affect settled allocations\"\n Balance Conservation: \"On-chain balances must always be greater than or equal to the sum of all accrued/claimable balances\"\n Non-negative Claimables: Claimables become zero when they should be positive\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n Implement Epoch-Based Weight Snapshots\n\nAdd a `weightsPerEpoch` mapping and snapshot mechanism to record voting weights at epoch boundaries:\n\n```solidity\n// In GaugeManager.sol - Add state variables\nmapping(uint256 => mapping(address => uint256)) public weightsPerEpoch; // epoch => pool => weight\nuint256 public lastSnapshotEpoch;\n\n// Add snapshot function called during notifyRewardAmount\nfunction _snapshotWeights() internal {\n    uint256 currentEpoch = HybraTimeLibrary.epochStart(block.timestamp);\n    if (currentEpoch > lastSnapshotEpoch) {\n        lastSnapshotEpoch = currentEpoch;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < pools.length; i++) {\n            address pool = pools[i];\n            weightsPerEpoch[currentEpoch][pool] = IVoter(voter).weights(pool);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunction notifyRewardAmount(uint256 _amount) external {\n    require(msg.sender == minter, \"!MINTER\");\n    \n    _snapshotWeights(); // ✅ Snapshot current weights before index update\n    \n    IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), _amount);\n    uint256 _ratio = _amount * 1e18 / IVoter(voter).totalWeight();\n    if (_ratio > 0) {\n        index += _ratio;\n    }\n    emit NotifyReward(msg.sender, base, _amount);\n}\n\n// Update _updateForAfterDistribution to use snapshot\nfunction _updateForAfterDistribution(address _gauge) private {\n    address _pool = poolForGauge[_gauge];\n    uint256 currentEpoch = HybraTimeLibrary.epochStart(block.timestamp);\n    uint256 _supplied = weightsPerEpoch[currentEpoch][_pool]; // ✅ Use snapshot\n    \n    if (_supplied > 0) {\n        uint256 _supplyIndex = supplyIndex[_gauge];\n        uint256 _index = index;\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = _index;\n        uint256 _delta = _index - _supplyIndex;\n        if (_delta > 0) {\n            uint256 _share = _supplied * _delta / 1e18;\n            if (isAlive[_gauge]) {\n                claimable[_gauge] += _share;\n            } else {\n                IERC20Upgradeable(base).safeTransfer(minter, _share);\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        supplyIndex[_gauge] = index;\n    }\n}\n```",
